  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "Let $X$ be the number of times a six is obtained when a regular die is rolled $n$ times. Suppose\n$$\\frac{\\Pr(X=4)}{\\Pr(X=5)}=\\frac{25}{4}.$$\nFind the value of $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=8$.\n\nSimplify the ratio of the two binomial probabilities.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\Pr(X=4)}{\\Pr(X=5)}&=\\frac{\\binom n4(\\frac16)^4(\\frac56)^{n-4}}{\\binom n5(\\frac16)^5(\\frac56)^{n-5}}\\\\\\frac{\\Pr(X=4)}{\\Pr(X=5)}&=5\\times\\frac{5}{n-4}\\\\\\frac{\\Pr(X=4)}{\\Pr(X=5)}&=\\frac{25}{n-4}.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{25}{n-4}&=\\frac{25}{4}\\\\n-4&=4\\\\n&=8.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
